<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram name="Data Model" id="log-data"><mxGraphModel dx="1900" dy="1400" grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1900" pageHeight="1400" background="#ffffff"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
<mxCell id="t" value="DISTRIBUTED LOGGING - Data Model (Cassandra + Elasticsearch + Kafka + S3)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a237e" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="20" width="1740" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="cassandraLabel" value="CASSANDRA (Hot/Warm Storage, Time-Series Optimized)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#e1bee7;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#7b1fa2;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="70" width="900" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="logsByService" value="TABLE: logs_by_service (Write-optimized, hot tier, 14-day TTL)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: (service_name, log_date), timestamp DESC, log_id&#10;  → Partition key: (service_name, log_date) -- all logs for payment_service on 2024-01-15 on same node&#10;  → Clustering key: timestamp DESC, log_id -- chronological order&#10;&#10;COLUMNS:&#10;  service_name    text      -- payment_service, auth_service, cart_service&#10;  log_date        date      -- 2024-01-15 (partition boundary)&#10;  timestamp       timestamp -- 2024-01-15 15:04:17.123 (event time, not ingest time)&#10;  log_id          uuid      -- unique ID for deduplication&#10;  log_level       text      -- DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR, FATAL&#10;  message         text      -- actual log message (up to 64KB)&#10;  host            text      -- server01.us-west-2.compute.internal&#10;  env             text      -- prod, staging, dev&#10;  namespace       text      -- kubernetes namespace (backend, frontend, analytics)&#10;  pod_name        text      -- payment-service-7f8d6c-abc123&#10;  trace_id        text      -- distributed tracing correlation ID (null if not present)&#10;  user_id         text      -- nullable, for user-specific logs&#10;  request_id      text      -- nullable, for request-scoped logs&#10;  metadata        map&lt;text,text&gt; -- key-value pairs (ip_address, user_agent, geo_country, etc)&#10;  created_at      timestamp -- ingest timestamp (when Flink wrote, for debugging lag)&#10;&#10;TTL: 14 days (USING TTL 1209600) -- rows auto-delete after 14 days without cleanup job&#10;&#10;QUERY PATTERN:&#10;  SELECT * FROM logs_by_service&#10;  WHERE service_name = payment_service AND log_date = 2024-01-15&#10;  AND timestamp &gt;= 2024-01-15 14:00 AND timestamp &lt; 2024-01-15 16:00&#10;  AND log_level IN (ERROR, FATAL)&#10;  ORDER BY timestamp DESC LIMIT 100;&#10;&#10;WHY THIS SCHEMA:&#10;  - Partition by (service, date): all logs for one service on one day on same node → fast range queries&#10;  - Clustering by timestamp DESC: chronological order, recent logs first (common query pattern)&#10;  - TTL auto-expires old data without manual DELETE jobs (critical at 1M writes/sec)&#10;  - Wide partition (1 service × 1 day): ~1-10M rows per partition (acceptable for Cassandra)&#10;  - Trace_id indexed separately for trace lookup (see logs_by_traceId table)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="120" width="900" height="520" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="logsByTrace" value="TABLE: logs_by_traceId (Distributed trace correlation)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: trace_id, timestamp DESC&#10;  → Partition key: trace_id -- single-partition lookup for all logs in one trace&#10;  → Clustering key: timestamp DESC -- chronological order&#10;&#10;COLUMNS:&#10;  trace_id        text      -- abc-123-def-456 (OpenTelemetry trace ID)&#10;  timestamp       timestamp -- event time&#10;  log_id          uuid      -- FK to logs_by_service (for full log details)&#10;  service_name    text      -- which service emitted this log&#10;  log_level       text      -- ERROR, INFO, etc&#10;  message         text      -- short message preview (first 200 chars)&#10;  span_id         text      -- OpenTelemetry span ID (for sub-operations)&#10;&#10;QUERY PATTERN:&#10;  SELECT * FROM logs_by_traceId WHERE trace_id = abc-123 ORDER BY timestamp;&#10;  → Returns all logs across all microservices for user request abc-123 in chronological order&#10;&#10;WHY SEPARATE TABLE:&#10;  - Trace lookup is a different access pattern than service+date lookup&#10;  - Single-partition read (trace_id) is faster than filtering logs_by_service across dates&#10;  - Only 20% of logs have trace_id; denormalizing avoids bloating main table" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="660" width="900" height="280" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="esLabel" value="ELASTICSEARCH (Hot Tier Search Index, 14-day ILM)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#fff9c4;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#f57f17;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="70" width="880" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="esMapping" value="INDEX: logs-2024-01-15 (daily rollover via ILM)&#10;&#10;MAPPING:&#10;  log_id          keyword   -- unique ID (no analysis, exact match only)&#10;  timestamp       date      -- range queries, aggregations by time bucket&#10;  log_level       keyword   -- term filter (ERROR, WARN, etc)&#10;  message         text      -- full-text search with standard analyzer (tokenize, lowercase, stem)&#10;  service_name    keyword   -- aggregations (count logs per service)&#10;  host            keyword   -- filter by server&#10;  env             keyword   -- filter by environment (prod, staging, dev)&#10;  namespace       keyword   -- kubernetes namespace filter&#10;  pod_name        keyword   -- container-specific logs&#10;  trace_id        keyword   -- exact match for trace correlation&#10;  user_id         keyword   -- filter by user (for GDPR deletion)&#10;  request_id      keyword   -- filter by request&#10;  metadata.*      keyword   -- dynamic mapping for metadata fields&#10;&#10;ILM POLICY (Index Lifecycle Management):&#10;  Hot phase (0-14 days):  Primary shards on SSD, full search enabled&#10;  Warm phase (14-30d):    Move to HDD, read-only, forcemerge to reduce segments&#10;  Delete phase (30+ days):Index auto-deleted (logs moved to Cassandra/S3 cold tier)&#10;&#10;QUERY EXAMPLE:&#10;  POST /logs-*/_search&#10;  {&#10;    query: { bool: { filter: [&#10;      { range: { timestamp: { gte: now-2h }}},&#10;      { term: { log_level: ERROR }},&#10;      { match: { message: NullPointerException }},&#10;      { term: { service_name: payment_service }}&#10;    ]}},&#10;    aggs: { errors_per_minute: { date_histogram: { field: timestamp, interval: 1m }}}&#10;  }&#10;&#10;WHY ELASTICSEARCH:&#10;  - Inverted index: word → log IDs (like book index) → sub-200ms full-text search&#10;  - Aggregations: count errors by service per hour = fast query (no GROUP BY scan)&#10;  - Multi-field search: proximity + text + filters combined in one query&#10;  - ILM auto-manages lifecycle (rollover, warm tier, deletion) without manual jobs" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffde7;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="120" width="880" height="520" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="kafkaLabel" value="KAFKA (Event Streaming Buffer)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#fff9c4;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#f57f17;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="660" width="420" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="kafka" value="TOPIC: raw_logs (ingestion buffer)&#10;&#10;Partitions: 100 (key: client_id hash modulo 100)&#10;Replication Factor: 3 (RF=3, min.insync.replicas=2)&#10;Retention: 7 days (logs kept for replay if Flink job fails)&#10;Compression: Snappy (3:1 ratio, CPU-efficient)&#10;&#10;Message Schema:&#10;  key:        client_id (string)&#10;  value:      JSON {log_id, timestamp, service_name, log_level, message, metadata, ...}&#10;  headers:    {schema_version: v2, agent_id: agent-abc-123, ingest_timestamp: epoch_millis}&#10;&#10;Producer Config (Ingestion Service):&#10;  acks=all (leader + 2 replicas must ack before success)&#10;  retries=3, retry.backoff.ms=100&#10;  max.in.flight.requests.per.connection=5 (pipelined for throughput)&#10;  compression.type=snappy&#10;&#10;Consumer Config (Flink):&#10;  group.id=flink-log-processor&#10;  enable.auto.commit=false (manual commit after Flink checkpoint)&#10;  auto.offset.reset=earliest (replay from beginning if no committed offset)&#10;  max.poll.records=10000 (batch processing for efficiency)&#10;&#10;TOPIC: alert_topic (alerting events)&#10;Partitions: 10 (key: alert_rule_id)&#10;Consumed by: Alert Service&#10;Retention: 24 hours (alerts processed quickly, no long-term storage needed)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="710" width="880" height="340" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="s3Label" value="S3 COLD STORAGE (Parquet, 45+ days)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#ffebee;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#c62828;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="970" width="420" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="s3" value="BUCKET: logs-cold-storage&#10;&#10;FORMAT: Parquet (columnar, compressed with Snappy, 3:1 ratio)&#10;PARTITIONING:&#10;  s3://logs-cold-storage/year=2024/month=01/day=15/service=payment_service/part-00001.parquet&#10;  → Athena query scans only needed partitions (year/month/day/service)&#10;&#10;PARQUET SCHEMA:&#10;  log_id          string&#10;  timestamp       timestamp&#10;  service_name    string&#10;  log_level       string&#10;  message         string&#10;  host, env, namespace, pod_name, trace_id, user_id, request_id, metadata (map)&#10;&#10;ATHENA TABLE:&#10;  CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE logs_cold (log_id string, timestamp timestamp, ...)&#10;  STORED AS PARQUET&#10;  LOCATION s3://logs-cold-storage/&#10;  PARTITIONED BY (year int, month int, day int, service_name string);&#10;&#10;QUERY EXAMPLE:&#10;  SELECT * FROM logs_cold&#10;  WHERE year=2024 AND month=01 AND service_name=payment_service&#10;  AND log_level=ERROR AND message LIKE %NullPointer%&#10;  LIMIT 1000;&#10;  → Scans only matching partitions, query completes in 10-30s&#10;&#10;LIFECYCLE:&#10;  - Cron job (daily 2 AM UTC) exports Cassandra rows older than 45 days to S3&#10;  - Parquet compression + partition pruning = $0.01/GB/month storage + fast Athena queries&#10;  - Glacier Deep Archive for compliance (7-year retention, $0.00099/GB/month, 12h retrieval)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1020" width="900" height="320" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="pgLabel" value="POSTGRESQL (Client + Alert Metadata)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#e1bee7;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#7b1fa2;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="1070" width="420" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="pg" value="TABLE: clients&#10;  client_id         uuid PRIMARY KEY&#10;  client_name       varchar(255) UNIQUE&#10;  token             text (JWT refresh token)&#10;  token_ttl         timestamp&#10;  env               varchar(50) (prod, staging, dev)&#10;  namespace         varchar(100)[]  -- allowed namespaces array&#10;  preferences       jsonb ({ retention_days: 90, sampling_rate: {DEBUG: 0.1, INFO: 0.5}, alert_channels: [email, slack] })&#10;&#10;TABLE: alert_rules&#10;  alert_id              uuid PRIMARY KEY&#10;  client_id             uuid REFERENCES clients(client_id) ON DELETE CASCADE&#10;  rule_name             varchar(255)&#10;  condition             jsonb ({ field: log_level, operator: =, value: ERROR, count: 100, window: 5m })&#10;  notification_channels jsonb ([ {type: email, address: oncall@company.com}, {type: slack, webhook: ...} ])&#10;  is_active             boolean DEFAULT true&#10;  cooldown_period       interval DEFAULT 10 minutes&#10;  last_triggered        timestamp&#10;  created_at            timestamp DEFAULT now()&#10;  updated_at            timestamp DEFAULT now()" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="1120" width="880" height="220" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="failures" value="FAILURE SCENARIOS&#10;&#10;1. Elasticsearch down during ingestion:&#10;   Problem: Flink tries to bulk index to ES → connection timeout/500 errors.&#10;   Solution: Flink publishes failed batches to es_retry Kafka topic (DLQ). Retry consumer reads from es_retry, retries with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s, ..., max 60s). If ES is down for hours, Kafka holds all logs safely (7-day retention). When ES recovers, retry consumer drains es_retry topic. Cassandra is source of truth; ES can be rebuilt from Cassandra if needed.&#10;&#10;2. Late-arriving logs (out-of-order):&#10;   Problem: Log from 3:04 PM arrives at 3:09 PM due to network delay or container restart. Without watermark, it would land in wrong time window → alert windows (ERROR count &gt; 100 in 5 min) would miscount.&#10;   Solution: Flink watermark = event-time - 5 min. Flink waits 5 min before closing a window. Log from 3:04 PM arriving at 3:09 PM: watermark at 3:09 is 3:04 → log is included in 3:00-3:05 window. Extremely late logs (10+ min) → Dead Letter Queue for manual investigation (rare: 0.01% of logs).&#10;&#10;3. Duplicate logs from agent retries:&#10;   Problem: Agent sends batch to Ingestion Service → network timeout → agent retries → same logs sent twice. Without deduplication, duplicate logs inflate storage by 30-40% and skew analytics.&#10;   Solution: Flink deduplication using 5-min tumbling window + hash(timestamp_minute + service_name + message[0:100]). Hash stored in RocksDB state backend. If hash exists → drop log; else → emit + save hash. Catches 99% of duplicates. Cross-window duplicates (same log 6 min apart) not detected (acceptable trade-off to keep state size bounded).&#10;&#10;4. Kafka partition skew (hot partition):&#10;   Problem: One client (client_id=ABC) generates 10x more logs than others → partition 42 (hash(ABC) mod 100 = 42) is overloaded → consumer lag on partition 42 increases.&#10;   Solution: Key by client_id + round-robin salt (0-9) → spreads one client across 10 partitions. Example: key = client_id + (timestamp mod 10). Trade-off: logs from one client are no longer in order across partitions, but Flink reassembles order using event-time watermark.&#10;&#10;5. Traffic spike during incident (alert storm):&#10;   Problem: Bad deploy → 1M ERROR logs in 1 minute → 1M alerts sent → alert fatigue, PagerDuty quota exceeded, engineers mute all alerts.&#10;   Solution: (1) Alert on aggregation: ERROR count &gt; 100 in 5 min (not individual ERROR). (2) Cooldown: 10 min before re-alerting same condition. (3) Deduplication: same fingerprint (service + error_type + hash(message[0:50])) → grouped summary alert (Top 10 error types, not 1M individual alerts). (4) Rate limiting: max 10 alerts per service per hour. (5) Auto-sampling during spike: DEBUG → 1%, INFO → 10%, ERROR → 100% (reduces volume by 80% while preserving error signal)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1360" width="1800" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="analogy" value="BEGINNER ANALOGY: The data model is a multi-tier filing system. Cassandra logs_by_service is the hot file cabinet (SSD) organized by service and date — every payment service log from Jan 15 is in the same drawer, sorted by time (clustering key timestamp DESC), with a 14-day expiry sticker (TTL). Elasticsearch is the card catalog (inverted index) where you can search for any keyword (NullPointerException) across all drawers in seconds. Kafka raw_logs is the incoming mail tray (buffer) that holds logs safely even if the filing clerk (Flink) is busy. S3 Parquet is the cold basement storage (cheap, slow) organized by year/month/day shelves with compression (Snappy) to save space. PostgreSQL alert_rules is the rulebook listing when to sound the alarm (ERROR count &gt; 100 in 5 min → page on-call engineer). Flink deduplication is the quality-control inspector removing duplicate letters before filing." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1f5fe;strokeColor=#0277bd;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1680" width="1800" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
